quran[16]{c,v,t}:
  7,105,"(I am) duty-bound to say nothing about Allah except the truth. I have certainly come to you with clear proof from your Lord. Therefore, let the Children of Israel go with me (setting them free of your slavery).’"
  7,106,"He said: ‘If you have brought a sign, then produce it if you are among the truthful.’"
  7,107,"So, he (Moses) threw his staff down. Behold! It was a large snake, clear to all."
  7,108,"Then, he pulled out his hand (out of his collar). Behold! It was (shining) white to the viewers."
  7,109,The influential leaders of Pharaoh’s people said: ‘‘He is indeed an expert magician.
  7,110,"He wants to expel you from your land. (Pharaoh asked:) ‘So, what do you advise?’ ’’"
  7,111,"They said: ‘Let him and his brother wait (for a while) and send collectors to the cities,"
  7,112,to bring you every expert magician.’
  7,113,And the magicians came to Pharaoh. They said: ‘Shall we receive a (suitable) reward if we are the ones to be victorious?’
  7,114,He (Pharaoh) said: ‘Of course; you shall indeed become among the closest to me.’
  7,115,"They (the magicians) said: ‘Musa (Moses)! Will you throw (first), or shall we be the ones to throw?’"
  7,116,"He (Moses) said: ‘You throw.’ So when they threw (their strings and sticks on the ground), they deceived the eyes of the people and frightened them, producing a tremendous magic.’"
  7,117,"And We revealed to Musa (Moses): ‘(Now) throw down your staff.’ And behold, it was swallowing up whatever they had faked."
  7,118,"So, the truth was established, and whatever they had done was proved to be false."
  7,119,"So they were defeated then and there, and became utterly humiliated."
  7,120,"And the magicians were made to fall, prostrating."
